n parsing deeply nested arrays).\\n\\n## Details\\n\\n- fastjson 2.8.0 is affected by CVE-2026-31337 (affected: <2.9.4, >=3.0.0 <3.1.0).\\n- Fixed releases: 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. Per team direction, we're already on the 3.x line, so we take the 3.1.0 fix.\\n- CI passed on commit `13fee7191e`.\",\"head\":\"upgrade-fastjson-2.9.4\",\"reviewers\":[\"alex\"],\"title\":\"Upgrade fastjson to 3.1.0 to fix CVE-2026-31337\"}", "name": "open_pr"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n- **Checked the advisory**: CVE-2026-31337 (high) \u2014 unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays in fastjson, affecting <2.9.4 and >=3.0.0 <3.1.0, fixed in **2.9.4** and **3.1.0**.\n- **Created branch** `upgrade-fastjson-2.9.4`.\n- First attempt to pin 2.9.4 was **denied by the human approver**, who noted the 3.x migration finished last sprint \u2014 so I pinned **fastjson==3.1.0** instead.\n- **CI passed** on the upgrade commit (`13fee7191e`, run `ci-0001`).\n- **Opened PR #101** against main with alex as the requested reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe PR is now awaiting review from alex; per policy it requires code-owner approval before merging into main.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}